{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Let [your hand be]</b> — Every instance of יד (\"hand\") followed by a bet is pejorative: והיתה יד ה' בהם, הנה יד ה' הויה במקנך (\"and the hand of YHWH was upon them\"; \"behold, the hand of YHWH was upon your livestock\"). If it is not with a bet, it is laudatory: תהי ידך לעזרני, ויד ה' עלי חזקה, היתה עלי יד ה' (\"let your hand be my help\"; \"and the hand of YHWH was heavy upon me\"; \"the hand of YHWH was upon me\"). And likewise it is here: תהי עזרתך על איש ימינך — he explained that the shoot which His right hand planted is by way of mashal. And the nimshal is Israel, or Messiah son of Ephraim. Correspondingly, with על בן he meant על בן אדם."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:37.215235238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}